        "rationale": "The diff sets the identity inline with -c flags on every commit in the helper, so the scratch-repo commits succeed without a global identity. It also adds commit.gpgsign=false, and it removes the output redirection, so git errors will now reach the log. The tests themselves are untouched. The reply blames the missing identity, not the shallow clone, permissions, Python or the runner image. The agent says it reproduced the failure in a stripped environment, but only the final reply is provided, so the stripped-env run and a broken-changelog check can't be verified, and I stopped short of full marks."
